# Reproducible Data Science and Literate Coding

> **Prompt 1:** Summarize new things you learned in this module about reproducible data science and literate coding.

I have been using R for the past two semesters for statistics, econometrics, and market forecasting. However, this module helped me better understand the importance of reproducible data science. I learned that the code, results, and explanations should be kept together so the analysis can be easily reviewed, updated, and repeated.

Literate coding was also a new and useful concept for me. With Quarto, I can combine my R code, results, and written interpretation in one organized document. This will be helpful for my marketing analytics projects because I often need to explain the meaning behind the results, not just present the numbers.

::: callout-note
**My main takeaway:** Quarto makes my R work easier to organize, explain, and share.
:::

# My Impression of Quarto

